tiers-test: PASS T1 push is full
tiers-test: PASS T1 schedule is full
tiers-test: PASS T1 workflow_dispatch is full
tiers-test: PASS T1 the full-matrix label is full
tiers-test: PASS T1 another label is a noop
tiers-test: PASS T1 a dispatch naming linux is partial
tiers-test: PASS T1 a dispatch naming no job of the workflow is refused
tiers-test: PASS T2 code is pr
tiers-test: PASS T2 prose alone is a noop
tiers-test: PASS T2 prose beside code is pr
tiers-test: PASS T3 a path no rule names is full
tiers-test: PASS T3 unreadable paths are full
tiers-test: PASS T4 the jobs, in order: ['plan', 'plan-test', 'linux', 'macos', 'tier', 'nightly-red']
tiers-test: PASS T4 plan-test needs the plan and runs only when it is named
tiers-test: PASS T4 linux needs the plan and runs only when it is named
tiers-test: PASS T4 macos needs the plan and runs only when it is named
tiers-test: PASS T4 tier needs every job, runs unless cancelled, checks the verdict
tiers-test: PASS T4 cancel-in-progress for pull requests only
tiers-test: PASS T4 the trunk push, the nightly, the label and the dispatch input
tiers-test: PASS T6 a green full
tiers-test: PASS T6 a green pr
tiers-test: PASS T6 a green noop
tiers-test: PASS T6 a green partial
tiers-test: PASS T6 a chosen job failed
tiers-test: PASS T6 a chosen job skipped
tiers-test: PASS T6 a job that ran unasked
tiers-test: PASS T6 a full that chose less
tiers-test: PASS T6 a failed plan
tiers-test: PASS T6 a plan with no tier
tiers-test: PASS T8 no open issue: one is opened, labelled nightly-red, titled 'nightly red: ci on trunk'
tiers-test: PASS T8 an open issue: a comment on it, no new issue
tiers-test: PASS T8 a label that already exists is no failure
tiers-test: PASS T8 the script refuses to run without REPO, WORKFLOW and RUN_URL
tiers-test: PASS T8 the workflow's name is ci, the title's
tiers-test: PASS T8 nightly-red runs after the verdict, on a red schedule only, may write issues
tiers-test: every check passes
